 suite or the web checks.\n\nBoth changes are in `src/sensei_top/api/dashboard.py`:\n- **Constant:** `CONTENT_SECURITY_POLICY` sits before `_SEPARATORS`, with a comment giving the reason for each directive. I split the string across two source lines to keep it within the line length; the value is the one in the spec.\n- **Split:** the old `get_response` body is now `_answer`. `get_response` calls it, sets the header and returns the response, and keeps its docstring.\n\n`LoopbackGuard` is untouched, so dashboard responses carry two CSP headers.\n\nA 404 raised under `/api` or `assets` propagates out of `_answer` before the header is set, so those errors don't get the policy.", "ttft_ms": 1890, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 17691, "uuid": "badf9dd4-d7c3-4ffe-a977-0c1ba0275101", "ttft_stream_ms": 1187, "time_to_request_ms": 55, "first_content_frame_ms": 1187, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
